  "body": "First slice of #743: **part 1 only** - the simulation draws the tool and its holder as a revolved body from the outline the collision laws judge.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `crates/app/src/sim_tool_body.rs`: `JudgedOutline` (the cutter-and-shank meridian of the judged tool record plus the holder bands), its revolved mesh, and `SimToolCache`.\n- The outline is assembled from the same two calls the fixture laws make (`tool_body::judged`, then `tool_body::stack`), so the drawn holder is the holder cylinder, an imported body's revolved envelope (#368) or a drawn holder's bands (#93, PR #475) - never a second derivation.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/world.rs` `sim_tool_tris` now draws that mesh, posed each frame by the frame's tip and tool axis (`sim::Frame::axis`, so tilted and 5-axis frames follow the axis). `State` gains `sim_tool_cache`.\n- The mesh is cached for the one tool at the playhead, keyed by its outline: rebuilt only when a judged number changes, dropped when the tool or operation is deleted, the tool is refused, or the transport closes.\n- A degenerate outline (non-finite, negative, running back down the axis, no radius, past the body caps) or a body that no longer fits its tool draws nothing and logs one named warning.\n- No new command or MCP tool: playback drawing is ephemeral. No law, verdict or posted output is touched.\n\n## Visible differences to expect\n\n- **A tool with an imported body** used to show the body's own facets (flats, slots, fixed turn). It now shows the body's revolved envelope bands.\n- **A drawn holder with a cone or an arc** is now drawn stepped: the laws read a cone as one cylinder at its larger end, and that cylinder is what the simulation shows. It looks coarser than the drawing in the tool editor (which is unchanged). This is the decision to look at first; see `docs/decisions/743-sim-revolved-tool-body.md`.\n- A bare tool (no body) looks as before.\n\n## How tested\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (app lib + `sim_tool_body`; ui lib + 10 gate-mapped ui suites; 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nPinning tests, `crates/app/tests/sim_tool_body.rs`:\n- `the_bare_tool_is_spun_from_the_cylinder_the_laws_sweep` - radii and extent from a known tool; the mesh's meridian is exactly the outline.\n- `a_modelled_body_is_drawn_as_its_judged_envelope_not_its_facets` - the drawn holder equals `tool_body::stack`'s bands; a hexagonal body is drawn at its envelope radius all the way round.\n- `a_drawn_cone_is_drawn_as_the_stepped_bands_the_laws_judge`\n- `the_body_follows_a_tilted_tool_axis` - every vertex keeps its height along, and distance from, a tilted, horizontal and flipped axis.\n- `a_degenerate_outline_draws_nothing_and_names_itself` - each refusal by name, a NaN draft without a panic, every catalog tool sane.\n- `a_body_that_no_longer_fits_draws_nothing_and_says_why`\n- `the_cached_mesh_is_reused_rebuilt_on_a_new_outline_and_freed_with_its_tool` - the mesh is freed on a new outline, on `DeleteOperation` and on `DeleteTool`.\n\nStructural UI test extended (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_body.rs`, `the_simulation_draws_the_tool_with_its_holder_cylinder_or_its_body`): the scene's tool part is the judged outline's mesh, and the cache empties when the transport closes. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **The on-screen look was not hand-checked** - the app was never launched. Shading of the stepped bands and the look of a tapered holder need the maintainer's eye.\n- No batch or release tier, no `--ignored` lanes.\n- A tilted axis is tested on the posed mesh, not through a generated 5-axis program in the UI.\n- A lathe insert tool at the playhead (draws nothing, marker only) is covered by code path only, not by a world-level test.\n- `tool_body_view::assembly_for_operation` / `bare_assembly` are left in place (their tests still pass) but the simulation no longer calls them.\n\n## Found and filed\n\n- #835 (P1, effort:high): a tool body is judged as two shapes - the fixture laws sweep the band stack (what is now drawn), the single-cylinder laws (shank/holder reach, probe) read the cylinder enclosing it. Not changed here.\n\n## Still owed on #743\n\n- Part 2, all of it: an imported STEP body converted to an editable half-profile on a centreline, stored as DXF; direct DXF half-profile import; our own DXF read/write with named refusals; the STEP -> DXF -> body -> DXF round trip. It overlaps open PR #602 and issue #361.\n- Part 1's \"hand-tested by the maintainer\".\n\nChangelog: The simulation draws the tool and holder as a revolved body from the same outline the collision laws judge (holder cylinder, body envelope or drawn holder bands), following the tool axis.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nRefs #743\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
